      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T17:37:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, I\u0027m really not sure. Either way isn\u0027t great. I am inclined to lean toward reporting the failure to the client, but even that doesn\u0027t prevent corruption because what if the failure is after a reboot, now you have a client not able to reclaim state. I guess another option would be to make such errors fatal, but I\u0027m not sure that can\u0027t get into a place where we lose data somnehow.\n\nI\u0027m going to hold off on merging this one, I think there\u0027s a bigger conversation and maybe it needs to happen on the IETF mailing list.",
      "parentUuid": "b8c3be4f_d8d1978d",
      "revId": "f26ce9d51b69a604907679db9446dcd6d3c1ecc3",
